[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds **412 unique reports** (the export has 427 rows; 15 ids
repeat). They are not one bug. They are three problems with three different fixes.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued fix covers only the first problem. It does not fix the other two.
</Callout>

## The three problems

| Problem | Reports | Ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **parser**: the shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates | 374 | [#7](https://github.com/skligerman/mega/issues/7) |
| **hint**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. Day-first people type it, and the form reads it their way | 33 | [#8](https://github.com/skligerman/mega/issues/8) |
| **shift**: the date is one day off, not swapped. Reports point at time zones | 5 | [#9](https://github.com/skligerman/mega/issues/9) |

374 + 33 + 5 = 412. Each report is counted once.

## What the desk's table shows

The table below is computed from the export. It splits by tenant and channel, so it shows
**379 parser** and **33 hint**. It files the 5 one-day reports under parser and footnotes them.
We count them once, in the shift ticket: 379 − 5 = 374.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## How to tell them apart

- **Do not use intake's tag.** It comes from the reporter's browser. It tags 42 reports as
  `hint`. Only 33 are.
- **Use the tenant and the channel.** Day-first tenant, form channel, booking-v3 form: hint.
  Day-first tenant, any other way in: parser.
- **Read the body for a shift.** Swapped day and month: parser or hint. One day off, with no swap:
  shift. The desk's own `oneDayMove` note names the 5 reports: R-41202, R-41209, R-41236,
  R-41344, R-41620.

## What we are not sure of

The shift cause is a lead, not proven. The reports mention June only, and a client in Lisbon
who got Tuesday while a client in Toronto got Monday. That looks like time zones. Four other
vague reports (R-41290, R-41417, R-41514, R-41615) stay in parser.

## Lessons

- Merging by subject line puts different bugs in one ticket. Read the body before you merge.
- Count once. A report that fits two causes still goes in one ticket.

